{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00119",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 1.15,
      "end_seconds": 4.52,
      "duration_seconds": 3.37,
      "text": "Hi, nice to see you. Sit down, please."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 5.91,
      "end_seconds": 9.23,
      "duration_seconds": 3.32,
      "text": "Thanks, doctor. It's been a long few days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 10.54,
      "end_seconds": 12.92,
      "duration_seconds": 2.38,
      "text": "Doctor, thank you for seeing us."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 13.22,
      "end_seconds": 14.57,
      "duration_seconds": 1.35,
      "text": "Busy day out there?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 15.33,
      "end_seconds": 18.4,
      "duration_seconds": 3.07,
      "text": "Always is. The traffic coming in was terrible."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 19.95,
      "end_seconds": 21.91,
      "duration_seconds": 1.96,
      "text": "Tell me what's been troubling you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 22.35,
      "end_seconds": 25.36,
      "duration_seconds": 3.01,
      "text": "Hmm, she's been having sneezing fits, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 28.98,
      "end_seconds": 31.21,
      "duration_seconds": 2.23,
      "text": "When did you first notice it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 31.57,
      "end_seconds": 38.73,
      "duration_seconds": 7.16,
      "text": "For two weeks, I'd say. I'd rather not end up on lots of tablets if I can avoid it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 40.9,
      "end_seconds": 42.92,
      "duration_seconds": 2.02,
      "text": "What makes it worse, if anything?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 43.76,
      "end_seconds": 46.27,
      "duration_seconds": 2.51,
      "text": "It's worse with dust and early mornings."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 47.32,
      "end_seconds": 50.0,
      "duration_seconds": 2.68,
      "text": "Anything that tends to go along with it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 51.18,
      "end_seconds": 62.84,
      "duration_seconds": 11.66,
      "text": "It usually comes with itchy watery eyes. Right, and there's a runny nose as well, six months now. The itchy watery eyes? That's been for about a week."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 63.15,
      "end_seconds": 65.62,
      "duration_seconds": 2.47,
      "text": "Do you notice anything setting it off?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 66.23,
      "end_seconds": 68.78,
      "duration_seconds": 2.55,
      "text": "I notice it more with pollen."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 69.15,
      "end_seconds": 73.02,
      "duration_seconds": 3.87,
      "text": "So, has there been a blocked nose at night too?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 77.45,
      "end_seconds": 80.46,
      "duration_seconds": 3.01,
      "text": "Yeah. One week, um, I'd say."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 80.87,
      "end_seconds": 81.57,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Any wheezing?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 81.96,
      "end_seconds": 83.88,
      "duration_seconds": 1.92,
      "text": "No wheezing, thank goodness."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 85.11,
      "end_seconds": 86.58,
      "duration_seconds": 1.47,
      "text": "Alright, what about fever?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 88.69,
      "end_seconds": 90.63,
      "duration_seconds": 1.94,
      "text": "No fever, thank goodness."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 91.23,
      "end_seconds": 95.17,
      "duration_seconds": 3.94,
      "text": "Actually, doctor, I did notice fever. She doesn't always say."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 95.99,
      "end_seconds": 101.44,
      "duration_seconds": 5.45,
      "text": "No, I don't think I did. Maybe a little, I'm not sure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 102.15,
      "end_seconds": 109.62,
      "duration_seconds": 7.47,
      "text": "Alright, I'll note both what you've said and what you've noticed. Any loss of smell, shortness of breath or facial pain at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 110.11,
      "end_seconds": 115.19,
      "duration_seconds": 5.08,
      "text": "I haven't had loss of smell, shortness of breath or facial pain, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 116.5,
      "end_seconds": 119.94,
      "duration_seconds": 3.44,
      "text": "What about your tummy and bowels, anything unusual there?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 120.89,
      "end_seconds": 123.08,
      "duration_seconds": 2.19,
      "text": "Nothing unusual, um, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 124.13,
      "end_seconds": 127.14,
      "duration_seconds": 3.01,
      "text": "Anything with your nerves, like weakness or numbness?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 127.82,
      "end_seconds": 129.7,
      "duration_seconds": 1.88,
      "text": "No, nothing like that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 130.96,
      "end_seconds": 134.6,
      "duration_seconds": 3.64,
      "text": "What about your general health, any conditions you're being treated for?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 134.95,
      "end_seconds": 152.19,
      "duration_seconds": 17.24,
      "text": "I, I have asthma, for nearly five years. I wasn't sure whether to come in at all, to be honest. A neighbour of mine said I should see someone about it. Eczema, for two years. My sister suggested writing things down, but I forgot."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 153.79,
      "end_seconds": 157.35,
      "duration_seconds": 3.56,
      "text": "Okay, asthma, that's already on your record. Good to know."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 158.21,
      "end_seconds": 160.72,
      "duration_seconds": 2.51,
      "text": "I want to open your previous notes quickly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 161.37,
      "end_seconds": 162.12,
      "duration_seconds": 0.75,
      "text": "Go ahead."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 174.39,
      "end_seconds": 177.91,
      "duration_seconds": 3.52,
      "text": "Okay, here we go. What medicines do you take regularly?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 179.46,
      "end_seconds": 184.28,
      "duration_seconds": 4.82,
      "text": "She is on hydrocortisone cream, when needed, I give it to her."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 184.78,
      "end_seconds": 185.73,
      "duration_seconds": 0.95,
      "text": "Any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 186.15,
      "end_seconds": 189.29,
      "duration_seconds": 3.14,
      "text": "Uh, no, never had any surgery."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 190.02,
      "end_seconds": 194.13,
      "duration_seconds": 4.11,
      "text": "Do you have any allergies to medicines, food, anything at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 195.37,
      "end_seconds": 196.09,
      "duration_seconds": 0.72,
      "text": "No allergies."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 197.42,
      "end_seconds": 200.5,
      "duration_seconds": 3.08,
      "text": "Let's get your blood pressure and the other basics."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 211.63,
      "end_seconds": 213.69,
      "duration_seconds": 2.06,
      "text": "Okay, give me a moment..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 230.24,
      "end_seconds": 239.16,
      "duration_seconds": 8.92,
      "text": "Okay: pulse is 80 beats a minute, oxygen saturation is 98 percent, blood pressure 115 over 76. And respiratory rate 14, temp 36.6 degrees."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 240.32,
      "end_seconds": 244.1,
      "duration_seconds": 3.78,
      "text": "Let me make a quick note of that before I forget."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 244.71,
      "end_seconds": 245.41,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Okay."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 257.12,
      "end_seconds": 258.58,
      "duration_seconds": 1.46,
      "text": "Okay, here we go."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 261.1,
      "end_seconds": 264.2,
      "duration_seconds": 3.1,
      "text": "I'll examine you now, so please bear with me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 265.04,
      "end_seconds": 268.49,
      "duration_seconds": 3.45,
      "text": "A little pressure here, tell me if it's tender."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 277.09,
      "end_seconds": 279.89,
      "duration_seconds": 2.8,
      "text": "The inside of your nose is pale and swollen."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 281.57,
      "end_seconds": 283.94,
      "duration_seconds": 2.37,
      "text": "Now I'm going to check this part."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 293.27,
      "end_seconds": 294.97,
      "duration_seconds": 1.7,
      "text": "Chest is clear, no wheeze."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 300.95,
      "end_seconds": 312.11,
      "duration_seconds": 11.16,
      "text": "That's fine, you can get dressed. Good, that's all I need to examine. Let me gather my thoughts and then we'll talk it through together. Is it okay if I type while we talk?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 312.76,
      "end_seconds": 315.03,
      "duration_seconds": 2.27,
      "text": "Yes, of course, go ahead."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 316.07,
      "end_seconds": 341.1,
      "duration_seconds": 25.03,
      "text": "From what you've told me and what I found, I think we're dealing with allergic rhinitis at this stage. I want to be honest that this is an impression, not a final answer. I can't rule out a viral cold yet. Let me just recap so I've got it right. You've had sneezing fits for two weeks, and no facial pain or wheezing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 343.35,
      "end_seconds": 344.57,
      "duration_seconds": 1.22,
      "text": "That's it, yes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0056",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 347.31,
      "end_seconds": 372.75,
      "duration_seconds": 25.44,
      "text": "Let's get an allergy test, for allergic rhinitis. I'll start you on levocetirizine, 5 milligrams, at night, for two weeks. It's for allergy symptoms. It's a commonly used medicine and most people tolerate it well. I'll start you on fluticasone nasal spray, 50 micrograms, one spray each side daily, for four weeks. That's for allergic rhinitis. Keep the windows closed in the early morning and wash the bedsheets weekly in hot water."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0057",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 373.16,
      "end_seconds": 387.6,
      "duration_seconds": 14.44,
      "text": "Make sure you're drinking plenty of fluids, two to three litres a day if you can, and get proper rest. Please don't sit on it if the symptoms get worse. That's the point to get seen urgently."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0058",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 392.07,
      "end_seconds": 393.65,
      "duration_seconds": 1.58,
      "text": "Got it, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0059",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 395.17,
      "end_seconds": 404.34,
      "duration_seconds": 9.17,
      "text": "I'd like to see you again in four weeks. Just so I know I've explained it clearly, can you tell me the plan back in your own words?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0060",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 405.08,
      "end_seconds": 415.9,
      "duration_seconds": 10.82,
      "text": "So, I take the levocetirizine, 5 milligrams, at night and take the fluticasone nasal spray, 50 micrograms, one spray each side daily. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0061",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 416.79,
      "end_seconds": 422.15,
      "duration_seconds": 5.36,
      "text": "Yes, exactly right. Good. Call the clinic if you need us in the meantime."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0062",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 423.1,
      "end_seconds": 425.79,
      "duration_seconds": 2.69,
      "text": "Uh, thanks so much, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0063",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 426.29,
      "end_seconds": 426.99,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Take care."
    }
  ]
}